# C: the Corporation's legal shell, its board, one acquired company and the events that shaped its portfolio.
nodes:
  - id: C:entity/mozilla-corporation
    type: entity
    name: Mozilla Corporation
    summary: 'California C corporation that makes Firefox and the services around it: announced in August 2005 as the taxable subsidiary of the Mozilla Foundation, held at 100% by the Foundation in the 2024 filings and, per the June 2026 Mozilla.org FAQ, owned by Mozilla.org. Headquartered in San Francisco with operations in Australia, Canada, China, New Zealand, the Netherlands, Germany, France, the United Kingdom and other European countries.'
    anchor: true
    form: corporation
    roles: [company, brand]
    jurisdiction: US-CA
    registered-office: 1875 Mission Street, Suite 103, San Francisco, CA 94103
    former-address: 149 New Montgomery Street, 4th Floor, San Francisco, CA 94105 (Form 990 Schedule R, 2024)
    domains: [firefox.com]
    global-id: {ein: 20-3226186, domain: firefox.com}
    tax-status: C corporation (taxable)
    fiscal-year: calendar
    since: 2005-08-03
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Foundation_Form_990_2024.pdf', 'https://assets.mozilla.net/annualreport/2024/b200-mozilla-foundation-form-990-public-disclosure-ty23.pdf', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Foundation', 'https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/legal/terms/mozilla/', 'https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/governance/organizations/'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:entity/anonym-inc
    type: entity
    name: Anonym, Inc.
    summary: Privacy-preserving digital advertising measurement company, previously headquartered in San Mateo, California; Mozilla acquired 100% of its stock on 2024-06-14. The Mozilla blog calls Anonym "a Mozilla confidential computing technology designed specifically for advertising analytics" (April 2026). A legal shell inside this atom.
    form: corporation
    roles: [shell, company]
    pending: Which Mozilla entity holds Anonym, Inc.? The audited statements say only "Mozilla".
    since: 2024-06-14
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://blog.mozilla.org/en/advertising/anonym-reddit-partnership/'], confidence: 0.8, state: known}

  - id: C:governance/board
    type: governance
    name: Board of Directors of Mozilla Corporation
    summary: One of the family boards named on the leadership page (with the Foundation, Mozilla.org and Mozilla.ai boards). Its size, composition and committees are not published on the pages read.
    voting-members: {pending: number of directors}
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/about/leadership/'], confidence: 0.6, state: known}

  - id: C:event/fakespot-acquired
    type: event
    name: Mozilla acquires Fakespot
    summary: 'On 2023-04-26 Mozilla acquired 100% of Fakespot, Inc. for cash and deferred contingent consideration: purchase consideration $27.4 million, of which $19.6 million goodwill.'
    kind: acquisition
    at: 2023-04-26
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fakespot'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/anonym-acquired
    type: event
    name: Mozilla acquires Anonym
    summary: 'On 2024-06-14 Mozilla acquired 100% of Anonym, Inc. for cash under 5% of total assets: purchase consideration $31.2 million (goodwill $19.1 million), plus a $44.4 million holdback that vests with continued employment over three years.'
    kind: acquisition
    at: 2024-06-14
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/mozilla-online-claims
    type: event
    name: Claims against Mozilla Online to wind it down
    summary: In May 2023 Mozilla filed legal claims against Beijing Mozilla Firefox Information Technology, Ltd. (Mozilla Online) with the long-term intent to wind down its operations in China. The contract with the Corporation expired without renewal; the litigation was still in process at 2024-12-31, and in March 2025 an arbitrator awarded Mozilla a portion of the amount it claimed.
    kind: dispute
    period: 2023-05
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/google-search-ruling
    type: event
    name: Mozilla comments on the US v. Google remedies ruling
    summary: 'Mozilla''s blog of 2025-09-08, a week after the remedies ruling: Google may not stop browsers from defaulting to or promoting other search engines or generative AI services; the court considered but rejected a ban on search payments to small independent browsers like Firefox.'
    kind: ruling
    at: 2025-09-08
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/internet-policy/defending-an-open-web/'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/pocket-shutdown
    type: event
    name: Pocket shut down
    summary: 'Announced 2025-05-22: downloads and new Premium subscriptions ended that day; Pocket shut down on 2025-07-08; saves could be exported until 2025-10-08, after which data was permanently deleted; annual Premium subscribers were refunded.'
    kind: retirement
    at: 2025-07-08
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/building-whats-next/', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pocket_(service)'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}

  - id: C:event/fakespot-shutdown
    type: event
    name: Fakespot shut down
    summary: The Review Checker built into Firefox ended on 2025-06-10; the Fakespot extensions, mobile apps and website stopped on 2025-07-01. The audited statements estimate a $13.7 million impairment on the acquired assets.
    kind: retirement
    at: 2025-07-01
    status: active
    visibility: public
    provenance: {mode: net-scan, sources: ['https://blog.mozilla.org/en/mozilla/building-whats-next/', 'https://stateof.mozilla.org/pdf/Mozilla%20Fdn%202024%20-%20AuditedFinancials.pdf'], confidence: 0.9, state: known}
